    "lawCode": "Add §827-a, Lab L",
    "lawSection": "Labor Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5202\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the labor law, in relation to granting a waiver of the\ncivil service examination fee to displaced homemakers\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\nTo remove the obstacle of civil service examination fees from\ndisplaced homemakers as they seek job opportunities and prepare to\nre-enter the workforce.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\nSection 1 of the legislation adds a new section 827(a) to the Labor\nLaw directing the commissioner of civil service, in consultation with\nthe state civil service department, to establish a program waiving the\ncivil service examination fee for persons who have successfully\ncompleted the displaced homemakers program or any job training program\nor opportunity provided by the multipurpose service center as\nestablished pursuant to Section 825 of this article.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThe displaced homemakers program and the job training program are both\ndesigned to help people re-enter the workforce by giving them the\nskills required to perform in jobs that will allow them to provide\nsubstantial means for themselves and their families. The training in\nthese programs will often provide quality skills specifically for\ncivil service positions; however, the persons completing these\nprograms are very often unable to pay the required examination fees\nfor civil service exams. This legislation would remove this obstacle,\nand allow for a smooth transition from the displaced homemakers\nprogram or job training program back to the workforce.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n2007-2008: A.5106 - Remained in Committee\n2006:      A.9662 - Remained in Committee\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nTo be determined.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect on the one hundred twentieth day after it\nshall become a law.\n",
